      "Explain web architecture, browser security boundaries, and common threat models.",
      "Recognize major vulnerability classes and their root causes.",
      "Design defensive authentication, session, authorization, input handling, API, file, and data-protection controls.",
      "Plan and run assessments only in authorized environments.",
      "Use code review, static/dynamic checks, and manual verification while accounting for tool limitations.",
      "Write sanitized reproducible reports and recommend root-cause fixes.",
      "Integrate security checks into development, release, and operational workflows.",
      "Design and demonstrate a secure application with testable security evidence."
